49.5: FINISHING (MOVEMENT) POSTURES Athletes must perform all five (5) Finishing movements. The 
Finishing has a maximum total score of 20 points (individual), or 5 points (duo). 
49.5.1: Finishing (movement) Postures: 1. Yang Sam Khum, 2. Payak Dom Kwang, 3. Kwang Liaw Lang, 4. Tad Mai 
Kom Nam and 5. Yang Suk Ka Sem. 
49.6: JOINING (CONNECTION) POSTURES Athletes can perform the Joining Postures (9). The Joining 
(connection) Postures have a maximum total score of 20 points (individual), or 5 points (duo). 
49.6.1: Joining (connection) Postures: 1. Sod Soi Mala, 2. Khuang Mad, 3. Muan Muay, 4. Chang Yaek Plok, 5. Klub 
Hua Sanam, 6. Klum Choeng Kru, 7. Doo Dussakorn, 8. Fon Long Choeng and 9. Kinaree Liab Thom. 
49.7: MAI MUAY AWARDING POINTS The Mai Muay has a maximum total score of 65 points. The Teams must 
forward their performances on the Jury Posture List form, to the Administration Jury no less than sixty (60) minutes 
before the start of the competition for inspection. All Muaythai Skill postures must be taken from the IFMA Khan syllabus 
and contain a blend of ‘Basic Skill’, ‘Art of Muay’ and ‘High Level’ posture groups. 
The following are guidelines for awarding points: 
49.7.1: Performance Realism A maximum total score of 30 points; 
49.7.2: Athlete Fitness A maximum total score of 25 points; and 
49.7.3: Other A maximum total score of 10 points. 
The following categories will be used to deduct points for minor infringements during Mai Muay contests: 
49.7.4: Timing Not too fast, not too slow; 
49.7.5: Target Correct target used for technique; 
49.7.6: Realistic Techniques used realistically; 
49.7.7: Balance Correct balance through-out; 
49.7.8: Continuality Fluid and does not pause; 
49.7.9: Conditioning Athlete looks strong at the end; 
49.7.10: Costume Remains in place throughout, and is IFMA approved; 
49.7.11: Spatial Awareness Full use within the competition area; and 
49.7.12: Posture List All postures on submitted Jury list completed. 
